<main>
<section class="hero">
  <div class="shell">
    <div class="eyebrow">Gwap Gang // Start Here</div>
    <h1>What Are You Trying To Improve?</h1>
    <p class="hero-copy">Pick the problem closest to the money. Gwap will route you to the smallest useful next move instead of burying you in tools, jargon, or a giant consulting menu.</p>
    <div class="hero-rule">
      <span>Choose the problem</span>
      <span>Get the right level of help</span>
      <span>Move with evidence</span>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section" id="routes">
  <div class="shell">
    <div class="section-head">
      <div>
        <div class="eyebrow">Choose A Lane</div>
        <h2>Start Where The Friction Is.</h2>
      </div>
      <p class="section-intro">These are the live Gwap paths available now. If you are unsure which one fits, start with the free diagnostic. It is designed to identify the commercial problem before asking you to buy anything.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="routes">
      <a class="route primary" href="{{ site.revenueLeakScore.salesUrl }}" data-route="growth-diagnostic">
        <div class="route-number"><span>01 // Diagnose Growth</span><span class="price">Free</span></div>
        <h3>I Need More Customers Or Better Conversion.</h3>
        <p>Run a bounded public-evidence Growth Diagnostic. Gwap looks for visible friction, ranks the strongest findings, and shows the most useful next move.</p>
        <div class="best-for"><strong>Best for</strong>You know growth could be better, but you do not yet know what is actually blocking it.</div>
        <div class="route-cta">Run My Free Growth Diagnostic →</div>
      </a>

      <a class="route" href="{{ site.revenueRescueSprint.salesUrl }}" data-route="revenue-rescue">
        <div class="route-number"><span>02 // Repair Revenue</span><span class="price">{{ site.revenueRescueSprint.priceLabel }}</span></div>
        <h3>I Know Something Is Leaking Revenue.</h3>
        <p>Get a fixed-scope Revenue Rescue Sprint focused on the three highest-value leaks, the evidence behind them, and a prioritized 7-day execution plan.</p>
        <div class="best-for"><strong>Best for</strong>You want a deeper diagnosis and a concrete repair sequence without signing up for an open-ended retainer.</div>
        <div class="route-cta">Explore Revenue Rescue →</div>
      </a>

      <a class="route" href="{{ site.primaryOffer.url }}" data-route="business-intelligence">
        <div class="route-number"><span>03 // Find Leverage</span><span class="price">$49</span></div>
        <h3>I Need Better Business Intelligence.</h3>
        <p>Get a practical AI Business Intelligence Report covering competitors, missed opportunities, AI leverage, revenue ideas, and a prioritized action plan.</p>
        <div class="best-for"><strong>Best for</strong>You need a broader strategic view of where technology, competition, automation, and revenue opportunities intersect.</div>
        <div class="route-cta">Get The $49 Intelligence Report →</div>
      </a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <div class="shell">
    <div class="section-head">
      <div>
        <div class="eyebrow">Explore Before You Buy</div>
        <h2>Follow The Signal First.</h2>
      </div>
      <p class="section-intro">You do not need to purchase anything to use Gwap. The editorial side exists to help you understand what is changing, what matters, and where leverage may be forming.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="secondary-grid">
      <div class="secondary-card">
        <div class="eyebrow">Free Intelligence</div>
        <h3>Read the thinking behind the products.</h3>
        <p>Use The Leverage Brief and the Gwap Intelligence Graph to explore the ideas, technologies, business models, and commercial opportunities Gwap is tracking.</p>
        <div class="link-row">
          <a class="acid-btn" href="/brief/">Read The Leverage Brief →</a>
          <a class="ghost" href="/graph/">Explore The Intelligence Graph →</a>
          <a class="ghost" href="/blog/">Browse All Intelligence →</a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="secondary-card">
        <div class="eyebrow">Next Capability</div>
        <h3>Search Intelligence.</h3>
        <p>A dedicated Gwap path for visibility, missed search demand, content gaps, index recovery, and opportunities to turn search behavior into commercial action.</p>
        <div class="coming">In Development // Not Yet Sold Here</div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <div class="shell">
    <div class="section-head">
      <div>
        <div class="eyebrow">How Gwap Works</div>
        <h2>Signal To Outcome.</h2>
      </div>
      <p class="section-intro">The products are different, but the operating logic stays the same. We look for evidence, turn it into a decision, and make the next action clear.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="process">
      <div class="step"><small>01 // Signal</small><h3>Find What Changed</h3><p>Behavior, competition, technology, search, conversion friction, or operational waste.</p></div>
      <div class="step"><small>02 // Intelligence</small><h3>Separate Signal From Noise</h3><p>Use evidence and business context to identify what deserves attention.</p></div>
      <div class="step"><small>03 // Action</small><h3>Choose The Move</h3><p>Prioritize by commercial impact, effort, speed, dependency, and risk.</p></div>
      <div class="step"><small>04 // Outcome</small><h3>Measure What Happened</h3><p>Keep what works, change what does not, and feed the result back into the next decision.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <div class="shell">
    <div class="boundary">
      <div class="boundary-grid">
        <div>
          <div class="eyebrow">Gwap Standard</div>
          <h3>Evidence Before Theater.</h3>
        </div>
        <div>
          <p>Gwap products are designed to distinguish observed evidence from estimates, assumptions, and recommendations. We do not invent lost-revenue numbers just to make a diagnosis sound more dramatic.</p>
          <p>When a higher-impact decision needs human judgment, the system should make that boundary visible instead of pretending automation is certainty.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="final">
  <div class="shell">
    <div class="eyebrow">Still Not Sure?</div>
    <h2>Start Free. Let The Evidence Decide.</h2>
    <p>If you do not know which Gwap product fits, the Growth Diagnostic is the correct first step. You will get a result before you are asked to make a larger commitment.</p>
    <a class="acid-btn" href="{{ site.revenueLeakScore.salesUrl }}">Run My Free Growth Diagnostic →</a>
  </div>
</section>
</main>

